UNIT defaultTo
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG defaultTo(value: any, defaultValue: any) -> any
DEPENDS-ON none

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEHAVIOR
# The complete source body is a single expression (verified byte-for-byte):
#
#     return (value == null || value !== value) ? defaultValue : value;
#
# Evaluate the guard with EXACT JavaScript operator semantics, in this order,
# with short-circuit OR:
#
#   NODE 1 (loose-null guard):  value == null
#     - Uses JS LOOSE equality (==), NOT strict.
#     - This is TRUE iff value is `null` OR value is `undefined`. No other
#       value is loosely-equal to null (per the ECMAScript abstract-equality
#       rules: null == undefined is true; null/undefined are == nothing else,
#       including 0, '', false, NaN, objects).
#     - If TRUE, short-circuits: the whole guard is TRUE (NODE 2 not evaluated).
#
#   NODE 2 (NaN self-inequality guard):  value !== value
#     - Only evaluated when NODE 1 is FALSE (value is neither null nor undefined).
#     - Uses JS STRICT inequality (!==).
#     - A value is strictly-unequal to itself IFF it is the primitive number NaN.
#       (NaN is the unique IEEE-754 value for which x !== x.) Every other
#       primitive, and every object reference, is strictly-equal to itself, so
#       this is FALSE for them.
#     - IMPORTANT NUANCE: a *boxed* NaN, e.g. `new Number(NaN)`, is an OBJECT.
#       NODE 1 is false (object is not == null) and NODE 2 is false (the same
#       object reference === itself). So a boxed NaN is NOT replaced -- it is
#       returned as-is. Only the PRIMITIVE NaN triggers replacement.
#       (This case is OUT-OF-ENVELOPE for the generator -- see SCOPE -- because
#       boxed primitives do not survive the oracle codec; it is documented here
#       so a blind re-emitter reconstructs it correctly.)
#
#   RESULT:
#     - If (NODE 1 is TRUE) OR (NODE 2 is TRUE)  ->  return defaultValue
#         i.e. value in { null, undefined, primitive-NaN }  ->  return defaultValue
#     - ELSE                                     ->  return value
#
# CRITICAL DETAILS / EDGE SEMANTICS (all verified against the real package):
#   - defaultValue is returned UNTOUCHED when selected. NO recursion, NO further
#     guarding. If defaultValue is itself null / undefined / NaN / an object,
#     that exact thing is returned. E.g. defaultTo(null, NaN) returns NaN;
#     defaultTo(undefined, undefined) returns undefined; defaultTo(null, null)
#     returns null.
#   - value is returned by IDENTITY (the same reference / same value) when kept.
#     Objects, arrays, Set, Map, Buffer/Uint8Array, RegExp are returned as the
#     same reference. defaultValue is likewise returned by identity.
#   - FALSY-BUT-PRESENT values are KEPT (returned as value), because they are
#     neither == null nor !== themselves:
#         0          -> kept (returns 0)
#         -0         -> kept; sign preserved (returns -0; Object.is(out,-0) true)
#         ''         -> kept (returns '')
#         false      -> kept (returns false)
#         0n (bigint)-> kept (returns 0n)
#         Infinity   -> kept (returns Infinity)
#         -Infinity  -> kept (returns -Infinity)
#   - ARITY: defaultTo(value) with NO second argument -> defaultValue is
#     `undefined`. So defaultTo(null) and defaultTo(undefined) and
#     defaultTo(NaN) each return `undefined` (the missing default). A present
#     value with one arg, e.g. defaultTo(0), returns 0.
#   - No throw paths exist. The function never throws for any argument shape
#     (it only reads via == / !==, which do not invoke user getters here since
#     no property access occurs; comparisons against null/self are total).
#   - PURE / READ-ONLY: no mutation of arguments, no ambient reads (no clock,
#     RNG, env, fs, net). No seam. Output is a pure function of the two args.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORACLE value -> oracle.json
# Deterministic value oracle: for each input tuple [value, defaultValue], the
# expected is whatever the real package returns (computed by the harness from
# the real package; the blind re-emitter reproduces it from BEHAVIOR above).

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE
# IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly):
#   The entire single-expression body above: the loose-null guard (== null),
#   the NaN self-inequality guard (!== self), short-circuit OR, ternary
#   selection, and return-by-identity of the selected operand.
#
# CARRIED DATA: none. No tables, no constants.
#
# DEMONSTRATED IN-SCOPE INPUT SUBSET (self-consistent with genInputs; every
#   value the generator can emit has its behavior defined above):
#   value-positions exercised: null, undefined, NaN (primitive), 0, -0, '',
#     false, 0n, Infinity, -Infinity, finite numbers, non-empty strings,
#     true, plain objects, arrays, RegExp, Set, Map, Uint8Array/Buffer, bigint.
#   defaultValue-positions exercised: numbers, strings, booleans, null,
#     undefined, NaN, objects, arrays, the same/other varied types.
#   Both directions of the codec-faithful matrix:
#     value in {null, undefined, NaN} -> expect defaultValue (returned as-is).
#     value otherwise                 -> expect value (returned by identity).
#
# OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (documented; NOT emitted by genInputs because they do not
#   round-trip through the oracle codec, but a blind re-emitter still
#   reconstructs their behavior from BEHAVIOR above):
#   - Functions and Symbols as value/defaultValue: not codec-faithful.
#       A function/symbol value is neither == null nor !== itself, so it is
#       KEPT (returned by identity). A function/symbol defaultValue is returned
#       as-is when selected.
#   - Boxed primitives (new Number(NaN), new String, new Boolean): not
#       codec-faithful (identity matters). As detailed in NODE 2: a boxed NaN
#       is an OBJECT and is KEPT (NOT replaced); only primitive NaN is replaced.
#
# OUT-OF-CONTRACT (stateful mutators / side APIs): none. Pure function.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROVENANCE
